ras3d (0.1.5-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * GRASS shim: add grass.pygrass.raster.RasterRow and
    grass.pygrass.raster.buffer.Buffer, and wire the pygrass submodules as
    attributes of their parents. Modules importing RasterRow could not be
    loaded in direct-file mode at all. RasterRow reads from the ras3d band
    cache where the name is present and fails loudly otherwise, rather
    than presenting an empty raster as a successful read; put_row() always
    fails, pointing at ras3d_write instead.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:04:27 +0100

ras3d (0.1.4-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * GRASS shim: add grass.script.mapcalc, grass.script.core and
    grass.script.utils (with a working get_lib_path), so modules that
    import them can be loaded in direct-file mode. mapcalc raises rather
    than returning silently, because there is no raster algebra outside
    GRASS and a no-op would leave an output map unwritten.
  * GRASS shim: expose grass.script's submodules as attributes of the
    parent as well as in sys.modules. "import grass.script.array as
    garray" resolves getattr(grass.script, 'array') before it consults
    sys.modules, so the attribute is what the import actually needs;
    i.hyper.specresamp and i.hyper.indices could not be imported at all
    without it.
  * test_ras3d_common.py: add load_addon(), which imports an addon whose
    filename contains dots via spec_from_file_location. The suites called
    importlib.import_module('i_hyper_<x>') for files named
    i.hyper.<x>.py, a name that can never resolve, so nine suites had
    never imported their module.
  * test_ras3d_common.py: resolve the shim from the source tree
    (RAS3D_SHIM_DIR, default ~/dev/libras3d/python) instead of the
    installed copy, which is root-owned and drifts behind the tree under
    test.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:56:57 +0100

ras3d (0.1.3-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Read band-separate GeoTIFFs (PlanarConfiguration=Separate with
    SamplesPerPixel=N in one directory, e.g. GDAL INTERLEAVE=BAND and
    ras3d's own 3-D output): the band count was taken from the number of
    directories, so such files opened as a single band.
  * Rewrite the GeoTIFF block reader: honour the requested x0/y0 window
    (it was ignored and full-width rows were written into the caller's
    buffer, overflowing it for any sub-window), leave cells outside the
    image null, and decode each tile or scanline once per call, scattering
    all requested bands. Pixel-interleaved files were decoded once per
    band (nbands times the file per read); a 1001x1001x255 cube now reads
    in about 1 s instead of 25 s.
  * test_write_georef: read the 3-D output back through ras3d and check
    multi-band sub-window reads, including cells beyond the image edge,
    on strip and tiled inputs.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:52:59 +0200

ras3d (0.1.2-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Fix 2-D GeoTIFF output (Rast_open_new + Rast_put_*_row): CELL rasters
    were written with the floating-point predictor, which libtiff rejects
    for integer samples, leaving empty strips (all-zero rasters). Use the
    horizontal predictor for integers; also set ImageLength and
    PhotometricInterpretation.
  * Georeference 2-D outputs from the current window: tie point, pixel
    scale and GeoKeys were never written.
  * Read the CRS (EPSG, geographic or projected) of GeoTIFF inputs and
    reuse it for 2-D and 3-D outputs; HDF5 inputs georeferenced from
    Lat/Lon arrays are tagged EPSG:4326. The 3-D writer previously never
    wrote a CRS and always declared a projected model.
  * Declare ExtraSamples on multi-band 3-D GeoTIFF outputs.
  * Add tests/test_write_georef.c, a self-contained test of values and
    georeferencing for CELL, FCELL and 3-D outputs (UTM and WGS84).

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:29:03 +0200

ras3d (0.1.1-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Add Python GRASS emulation layer (ras3d_grass_shim.py): drop-in
    replacement for grass.script used by i.hyper.* modules; provides
    gs.parser(), gs.raster3d_info(), gs.run_command() and all logging
    functions without requiring a GRASS installation.
  * Add GeoTIFF/3D output helpers (ras3d_write.py): write_raster2d(),
    write_raster3d(), outpath() backed by GDAL for LZW-compressed output.
  * Add test_ras3d_common.py: shared pytest fixtures and helpers for
    i.hyper.* standalone test suites (open_cube_checked, assert_band_valid,
    make_wl_sidecar, skip markers for data availability).
  * libras3d-python: now ships all three Python modules.
  * Fix pkg-config includedir (was /usr/ instead of /usr/include) by
    moving include(GNUInstallDirs) before configure_file() in CMakeLists.
  * Fix private lib in ras3d.pc: use hdf5_serial (Debian trixie name).
  * Add missing GRASS API stubs: G__gisinit, G_add_keyword, G_get_window,
    G_percent, G_debug, G_verbose_std, Rast3d_init_defaults,
    Rast3d_min_unlocked, struct Cell_head, GPATH_MAX, M_PI.
  * Correct Rast3d_open_new_opt_tile_size to actual 5-arg GRASS signature.
  * i.hyper.atcorr: DEBIAN_BUILD=1 Makefile mode tested and confirmed.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Sat, 10 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000

ras3d (0.1.0-1) trixie; urgency=low

  * Initial release.
  * GeoTIFF backend: tiled/strip, contiguous/separate planar, any bit depth.
  * HDF5 backend: auto-probe for radiance/reflectance datasets;
    RAS3D_HDF5_DATASET override; geo-extent from Lat/Lon arrays.
  * Drop-in GRASS API: Rast3d_*, G_*, Rast_*, G_parser emulation.
  * OpenMP parallelism for compute; serial HDF5 I/O (thread-safety).
  * Python ctypes wrapper (libras3d-python package).
  * i.hyper.atcorr integration via HAVE_RAS3D compile-time guard.

 -- Yann Chemin <dr.yann.chemin@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
